Per-section byte breakdown for the imac_g3 d=2.5 -> d=3.0 wedge investigation.

Source image:
  /home/lilith/work/codec-corpus/gb82-sc/imac_g3.png (2940x1912 RGB8 PNG, 689345 bytes)

Encoders:
  cjxl v0.12.0 4279d48 (libjxl, /home/lilith/work/jxl-efforts/libjxl/build/tools/cjxl)
  ours: jxl-encoder HEAD (commit a3b27b5), target/release/cjxl-rs, default effort 7

Commands:
  cjxl -d {2.5,3.0} -e 7 imac_g3.png cjxl_d{2.5,3.0}.jxl
  cjxl-rs -d {2.5,3.0} --effort 7 imac_g3.png ours_d{2.5,3.0}.jxl

Parser: /tmp/jxl_toc_dump (Rust binary using jxl-oxide's Bitstream + Toc parser,
        iterates frames until is_last=true, reports per-frame TOC section sizes).

Findings:
  * cjxl @ d=2.5: NO patches reference frame (single RegularFrame, 376KB total)
  * cjxl @ d=3.0: PATCHES enabled (32KB ReferenceOnly + 129KB main, 162KB total)
  * ours @ d=2.5: 88KB patches ref frame + 145KB main = 234KB
  * ours @ d=3.0: 88KB patches ref frame + 135KB main = 224KB (essentially identical patches)
  * cjxl ref frame is single-section (group_size_shift=2 -> 512-pixel groups, 1 group fits)
  * ours ref frame is 4 sections (group_size_shift=1 -> 256-pixel groups, 2x2 groups)
  * Ours patch set is IDENTICAL between d=2.5 and d=3.0 (already established by W41-2 commit 0c3ccc96)

Verification of cjxl's d=2.5 -> d=3.0 cliff:
